---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { url } from '../lib';

// Words from Lila (approved 2026-10-19); change them only with her OK.
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Who writes Sigil & Silicon, where the old posts came from, and how new posts get written."
>
  <article>
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      Sigil &amp; Silicon is my blog: old magic, new circuits, and whatever else strikes my
      fancy. I'm Lila (most people offline know me as Lena), and I write about the occult and my
      spiritual path, AI and the things I build with it, being trans, and whatever film or rabbit
      hole has my attention at the moment.
    </p>
    <p>
      The posts from 2013 to 2018 came over from Blogger, where this blog used to live as The
      Sound Of Sweating Silicon. They're kept here as I wrote them.
    </p>
    <p>
      Newer posts are written with Claude. The ideas are mine, usually worked out in long
      conversations; Claude drafts the post in a voice we built from my own writing; I read it and
      push back, and nothing goes up until I'm happy with it. Facts get checked and linked where I
      can, and when a specific idea in a post came from Claude rather than from me, the post says
      so where it comes up.
      "<a href={url('posts/picking-this-back-up/')}>Picking This Back Up</a>" explains why I write
      this way now.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
